    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm 72 and i just had a really scary moment. i went to stand up from my chair and everything just went black for a few seconds. i felt like i was going to pass out. i'm also noticing my heart is fluttering a bit and feels like it's skipping beats. i really don't want to go to the ER if i can help it, it's such a hassle. do you think i could just take some magnesium or maybe an extra dose of my vitamins to help steady my heart rhythm? what's a good amount to take so it stops acting up?",
